<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/twelver-shiism"><span class="enc-name">Twelver Shi'ism</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Twelver Shi'ism is the largest branch of Shia Islam, recognising a line of twelve imams, the last of whom is believed to be in occultation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Twentieth Dynasty of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Twentieth Dynasty of Egypt was the last royal dynasty of the New Kingdom, ruling in the twelfth and eleventh centuries BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/twenty-fifth-dynasty-of-egypt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/twenty-fifth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Twenty-fifth Dynasty of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Twenty-fifth Dynasty of Egypt was a line of Kushite kings from Nubia who ruled Egypt in the eighth and seventh centuries BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/twenty-seventh-dynasty-of-egypt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/twenty-seventh-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Twenty-seventh Dynasty of Egypt</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Twenty-seventh Dynasty of Egypt is the name given to the first period of Persian rule over Egypt, beginning with Cambyses II's conquest in 525 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/twenty-sixth-amendment-of-the-constitution-of-india"><span class="enc-name">Twenty-sixth Amendment of the Constitution of India</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Twenty-sixth Amendment of the Constitution of India, enacted in December 1971 under Indira Gandhi, abolished the privy purses paid to the former rulers of the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/two-ewalds"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/two-ewalds.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Two Ewalds</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">The two Ewalds, called Ewald the Black and Ewald the Fair, were English priests who went as missionaries to the Old Saxons around 695.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/two-towers-bologna"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/two-towers-bologna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Two Towers (Bologna)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Two Towers, the Asinelli and the Garisenda, are medieval towers in the centre of Bologna, Italy, and the city's best-known landmarks.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyana"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyana</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tyana was an ancient city of southern Cappadocia in central Anatolia, at modern Kemerhisar near Niğde.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyburn"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyburn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyburn</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tyburn was a village west of London, near today's Marble Arch, whose name became a byword for execution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/image