he Inn, Adige and Eisack and the Brenner Pass.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyrol-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyrol-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyrol Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Tyrol Castle stands above Merano in South Tyrol, Italy, and was built in the early 12th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyrrhenian-sea"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyrrhenian-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyrrhenian Sea</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tyrrhenian Sea is the part of the Mediterranean bounded by mainland Italy, Sicily, Sardinia and Corsica, named from the Greek word for the Etruscans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyrtaeus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyrtaeus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyrtaeus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Tyrtaeus was a Greek elegiac poet who lived in Sparta in the mid-seventh century BCE, during the Second Messenian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tyumen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tyumen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tyumen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Tyumen is a city in western Siberia, Russia, on the Tura river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/tzutujil-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tzutujil-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Tz'utujil people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Tz'utujil